  "id": "COMPOUND:24007 - PROTEIN:4983",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 4-Prop-2-Enoxychromen-2-One is a target of multiple entities that ultimately lead to Jurkat. This compound is linked to the Werner syndrome ATP-dependent helicase, which is a key enzyme in DNA repair and aging. The helicase is also targeted by another compound, 19-Oxo-3-beta,5,14-trihydroxy-5-beta-bufa-20,22-dienolide-3-acetate, which in turn targets Jurkat. Additionally, 4-Prop-2-Enoxychromen-2-One is associated with WM-115, which is targeted by Sucutinirane F, also leading to Jurkat. These findings suggest a potential pathway where 4-Prop-2-Enoxychromen-2-One may influence Jurkat through its interaction with these target proteins, possibly via a common mechanism involving DNA repair or cellular processes. The integration of these targets highlights a possible role for 4-Prop-2-Enoxychromen-2-One in modulating cellular functions that are relevant to Jurkat, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
